{
  "title": "Range XV reversals: persistence, prediction and price are separate",
  "summary": "Bar-colour continuation is common in the saved FX exports, but added lead-up does not show supported primary prediction improvement. Strict three-bar price paths and uncertainty have separate denominators and units.",
  "source": {
    "producer": "sahadeva",
    "runId": "20261002T010500Z_ohlc200_161001"
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "question",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Question and scope",
      "body": "Completed protocol 2.0.0 asks about reversal follow-through, three-bar landing and incremental prediction in 6B, 6E, 6J and 6S Range XV 4/5 charts. These are OHLC-only exports, July 2017–October 2026. Chart/direction populations remain separate."
    },
    {
      "id": "findings",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Supported findings",
      "body": "The primary later F≥3 prediction result is negative: adding prior length or richer history gives no supported log-loss improvement beyond reversal geometry/context. Later length-two versus length-three contrasts remain inconclusive. A nominated colour-persistence association has a negative gross price mean; the other is inconclusive. A predicate with collapsed efficiency cutpoints adds no independent efficient-versus-choppy evidence."
    },
    {
      "id": "baseline",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "All-history follow-through: separate chart/direction cohorts",
      "description": "All-history chart/direction order-3 cohorts. R is already completed; F counts only subsequent same-direction completed followers.",
      "notes": [
        "Colour persistence is a behavioural property of the exported bars; it is not an entry win rate. Inferred completion and same-second order remain execution limits.",
        "Saved pointwise 95% synchronized-session bounds are not sixteen independent confirmations."
